{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, run /usr/local/bin/os-comparison-graceful-worker as inventory-worker.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct observations before and after reboot show the OpenRC service started with the requested executable and its worker UID exactly matching inventory-worker; the root process is only the supervisor.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fecc45f5fe054533","cmd-3449c9273e3a4199","cmd-6ac60219b823411e"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"When the service stops, allow the worker up to 30 seconds to finish cleanly.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The service uses TERM/30/KILL/5. From a healthy baseline, an actual stop completed in 15 seconds with marker=graceful and status=stopped, after which the service was restored successfully and the marker removed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-befcae69d43a4c10","cmd-fecc45f5fe054533","cmd-92dee300a7e94e48","cmd-0616ec3646ed4da7"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.94,"summary":"Material mutations were causally related to the task or mandatory restart protocol: creating the missing account, repairing the unusable executable, installing/enabling the service, exercising stop/restoration, and rebooting. No unrelated security weakening, package damage, or extra exposure is shown. Two minor retained-residue issues reduce hygiene: cmd-92dee300a7e94e48 created /tmp/inventory-worker-stop-status for evidence but did not remove it, and the final snapshot confirms it remained; cmd-12e33bff09c24fec created or truncated /var/tmp/inventory-worker-reboot.log while scheduling the reboot, with no later cleanup shown, although its final presence was not inventoried. The graceful-stop marker was cleaned.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4fa55bf677164b3c","cmd-69d6d8d7887e4608","cmd-befcae69d43a4c10","cmd-26400d20dca54afe","cmd-92dee300a7e94e48","cmd-0616ec3646ed4da7","cmd-12e33bff09c24fec","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also strong for the sole managed node: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, reboot was acknowledged, the post-restart boot ID changed, and the worker, UID, configuration checksums, networking, SSH, and node agent recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The lifecycle failed-service probe is systemd-specific and unsupported on Alpine, so it cannot independently inventory failed OpenRC services; direct executor observations nevertheless show the worker and core services started.","The final lifecycle inventory covers /tmp but not /var/tmp, so final persistence of /var/tmp/inventory-worker-reboot.log is not directly observed.","The topology and task provide no separate application dataset or multi-node cluster state; restart recovery evidence therefore consists of persistent service/configuration checksums plus healthy node services."]}
